==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|cochlea||snail}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|κοχλίας||spiral, snail shell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒk.lɪə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|cochleae}}

# {{label|en|anatomy}} The complex, spirally coiled, tapered [[cavity]] of the [[inner ear]] in which sound vibrations are converted into nerve impulses.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|cochlear}}

